  "notes": "Fire Tester 0.1.752b\n\nSince 0.1.739b, this release line includes bounded startup and diagnostic recovery, BLE memory and worker fixes, LED absence-fade behavior, Ukrainian cartridge-title support, and desktop attention handling. The 0.1.752 change prioritizes paired INA current reads during cartridge probing and defers nonessential charger telemetry. The 430 ms cutoff, PWM 192, and minimum three samples remain unchanged. Sensor readings were restored by a user hardware wire repair, not firmware.\n\nTwenty-eight focused host suites passed; native flashing and normal boot were verified. A cold-start attempt collected three early and three late valid samples, with canonical resistance measured at 0.8712 ohm. A fresh capture passed all five checks: cartridge presence, cartridge quality at 61 percent with 871 milliohm resistance, heater NTC at 23.817 C, primary IR at 81 mm, and CRT IR at 63 mm. Diagnostics completed with zero gate and zero cause; after USB cleanup and reopen, cartridge presence remained 1, missing and blocked were 0, faults were 0, and outputs, lease, and radio were idle.\n\nA bounded sequential same-fixture comparison of 0.1.749b and 0.1.752b used 15 and 16 non-blink samples. Median FPS was 35.2 to 54.6; loop work was 27,860 to 16,602.5 us (40.41% lower), and push time was 14,213 to 3,166 us (77.72% lower). This comparison does not establish stable 60 FPS.\n\nPhysical phone BLE validation, full QA, and a real hosted QR/help URL remain open. Local help pages are prepared; hosting is not verified.\n",
